<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 39,861 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 39,861 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 39,861 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday, compared to 91,869 tonnes on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Saturday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			26,388	    32,913</p>
<p>    Import cargo			13,473	    58,983</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight ships are expected to sail and eight to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		 78,750	 Chesa Peak	   due</p>
<p>Sugar		   3,000	  Panormos Wind	30/3</p>
<p>Crude oil	     70,000	 Stavros-1	    31/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
